  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Crossover school – round the cone and zigzag",
  "description": "Start standing still: lift the left skate over the right so you move sideways to the right, 4–6 times, then the other way. Then pick up speed and do 2–3 crossover strides to the right, then to the left.\n\nPut out one cone for every 2–3 players. The players circle the cone with crossovers 10–15 times one way, then as many the other way. Then a line of cones 5–7 metres apart: the players skate a zigzag, rounding every other cone on the outside with a couple of crossovers in each turn.\n\nWhen it goes well the players take a ball, and then the speed goes up. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Bend the knee deeply as the skate crosses over."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Straight back and the upper body turned slightly into the turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Stick in one hand in front of the body, towards the way you turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Practise both directions equally."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
